1
00:00:00,593 --> 00:00:02,093
(Bernadette(on phone):)Long story.

2
00:00:02,094 --> 00:00:03,624
(Bernadette(on phone):)Why don't you go ahead and eat.

3
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:04,929
(Bernadette(on phone):)We're gonna be a while.

4
00:00:09,168 --> 00:00:11,438
(Howard:)I'm telling you,
I'm not on drugs.

5
00:00:11,437 --> 00:00:14,437
The government's out to get me!

6
00:00:17,176 --> 00:00:20,046
(Alfred:)Now, one of the more exciting
things to be found recently

7
00:00:20,046 --> 00:00:21,576
(Alfred:)is that Neanderthals

8
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,980
(Alfred:)and Homo sapiens frequently
mated with each other.

9
00:00:24,984 --> 00:00:28,354
(Mary:)Well, that certainly explains
my marriage to Sheldon's father.

10
00:00:28,354 --> 00:00:30,124
(laughs)

11
00:00:31,357 --> 00:00:35,097
(Sheldon:)That's funny, because my father
was not a very clever man.

12
00:00:35,961 --> 00:00:37,761
(Amy:)I'd be lost without you.

13
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:40,969
(utensil clinking on glass)

14
00:00:40,966 --> 00:00:43,166
(Leonard:)Uh, I would like
to propose a toast

15
00:00:43,169 --> 00:00:45,069
(Leonard:)to my wife and bride-to-be.

16
00:00:45,071 --> 00:00:46,341
(Sheldon:)See, that's funny because...

17
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:47,508
(Amy:)Back to your phone.

18
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:52,172
(Scene:)Penny...

19
00:00:52,178 --> 00:00:54,248
(Leonard:)I've always known I loved you,

20
00:00:54,246 --> 00:00:56,746
(Leonard:)but this last year has shown me

21
00:00:56,749 --> 00:00:58,979
(Leonard:)that I also love
being married to you.

22
00:00:58,984 --> 00:01:01,484
(Leonard:)Thank you
for saying yes.

